<title>JAPAN: Japan govt should decide on intervention - PM group.</title>
<headline>Japan govt should decide on intervention - PM group.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A decision to intervene in currency markets should be left mainly to the Japanese government rather than the Bank of Japan, the head of a study group under Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto told reporters on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The group is studying revisions on the law governing the central bank.</p>
</text>
